{"type":"npc","name":"Trench Lord","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":280,"temp":0,"max":280,"details":""},"ac":{"value":35,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":20,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"swim","value":100}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"bleed","exceptions":[]},{"type":"fire","exceptions":[]},{"type":"paralyzed","exceptions":[]},{"type":"poison","exceptions":[]},{"type":"sleep","exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"acid","value":10,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["thalassic"],"details":""},"level":{"value":14},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>In the deepest reaches of the ocean, where the pressure would crush most creatures and light is an alien concept, elementals known as trench lords reign above their lesser kin.</p><p>Trench lords typically live around hydrothermal vents, with boiling temperatures, toxic chemicals, and immense pressure found in the deepest waters, making their homes inhospitable to nearly all others. They often go centuries without encountering another sapient being, peacefully enjoying the ocean currents. When they do encounter creatures from the surface, they stealthily observe them and take violent action at the slightest hint that these strange beings might endanger the environmental balance of their oceans.</p><p>The few trench lords that don't dwell in the deep sea live in environs with similar conditions, such as active volcanoes becoming fledgling islands, hot springs, and pressurized vats used in mass alchemical production. Such trench lords are often more varied in behavior; one in a hot spring might enjoy the company of humanoids, while one newly formed from volcanic activity might be aggressive toward all life.</p><h2>It Takes Two</h2><p>While a single trench lord tries to preserve the status quo in the oceans and is a force for stability, two trench lords in close proximity can breed wholesale destruction. When these two usually solitary creatures discover the joys of communication—or the anguish of forced contact with an enemy—they often begin to engineer the birth of other trench lords by causing underwater eruptions, either to create new friends or to recruit allies in their battle with their rival. Several volcanic archipelagos began as the joint project of two trench lords.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 560/1,250/2,300 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), perception item, skill items (Athletics, Lore [Deep Sea], Nature, Stealth)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> body, bane, burning barbs, dexterity, elongating, energy resistant (acid, fire, vitality), fire, fire shield, poison, poisonous armor, strength, throwing, water, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Nathan Wright","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":9},"dex":{"mod":7},"con":{"mod":6},"int":{"mod":0},"wis":{"mod":5},"cha":{"mod":0}},"perception":{"details":"heatsense (imprecise) 120 feet","mod":24,"senses":[],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":25,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":28,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":22,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"athletics":{"base":28},"nature":{"base":23},"stealth":{"base":25}},"traits":{"value":["aquatic","elemental","water"],"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"grg"}}},"_id":"aNpCv8zW8bJGTH47","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/trench-lord.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Trench Lord","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":4,"height":4,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/trench-lord.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":2,"scaleY":2,"rot